From: Reproducible AI <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] references/classification: allow --resume to read our own checkpoints

train.py pickles the run's argparse.Namespace into every checkpoint under the
"args" key (see the checkpoint dict built in main()), but loads checkpoints with
torch.load(..., weights_only=True).  Since PyTorch 2.6 that unpickler refuses any
global that is not explicitly allow-listed, and argparse.Namespace is not one, so
every --resume and every --test-only --resume raises:

    _pickle.UnpicklingError: Weights only load failed.
      WeightsUnpickler error: Unsupported global: GLOBAL argparse.Namespace was
      not an allowed global by default.

The only producer of these files is train.py and the only consumer is train.py,
so the documented resume path cannot round-trip on any currently supported
PyTorch.  Reproduced on torch 2.7.0 with a checkpoint written by train.py itself.

Allow-list argparse.Namespace for this one load.  The scope is limited to the
resume call, so no other torch.load in the file is loosened, and the checkpoint
format is unchanged (existing checkpoints keep working).

An alternative fix is to stop writing "args" into the checkpoint at all -- it is
never read back; the load below only touches "model", "optimizer",
"lr_scheduler", "epoch", "model_ema" and "scaler".  That is the tidier change but
it breaks anyone who reads args out of an existing checkpoint, so the
conservative fix is proposed here.

NOT SUBMITTED UPSTREAM.

---
diff --git a/references/classification/train.py b/references/classification/train.py
--- a/references/classification/train.py
+++ b/references/classification/train.py
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+import argparse
 import datetime
 import os
 import time
@@ -339,7 +340,10 @@
         model_ema = utils.ExponentialMovingAverage(model_without_ddp, device=device, decay=1.0 - alpha)
 
     if args.resume:
-        checkpoint = torch.load(args.resume, map_location="cpu", weights_only=True)
+        # train.py stores the run's argparse.Namespace under "args"; weights_only
+        # unpickling rejects it unless it is explicitly allow-listed.
+        with torch.serialization.safe_globals([argparse.Namespace]):
+            checkpoint = torch.load(args.resume, map_location="cpu", weights_only=True)
         model_without_ddp.load_state_dict(checkpoint["model"])
         if not args.test_only:
             optimizer.load_state_dict(checkpoint["optimizer"])
